      "stdout": "Add tone/voice metadata to a text segment.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT       Target segment id (required; raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --text TEXT         Optional text override; defaults to target segment content\r\n          --speed TEXT        Playback / synthesis speed, e.g. 1.0\r\n          --emotion TEXT      Emotion tag, e.g. happy\r\n          --audio-path TEXT   Existing/generated tone audio path\r\n          --resource-id TEXT  Tone/voice material resource id\r\n          --network-mode TEXT Network adapter mode, e.g. real / mock / offline\r\n          --output-dir TEXT   Directory for generated audio output\r\n          --audio-format TEXT Generated audio format, e.g. wav / mp3\r\n          --write-to-draft TEXT \r\n                              Write generated audio into the draft: true / false\r\n          --copy-to-draft TEXT \r\n                              Copy generated audio into the draft workspace: true / false\r\n          --start-time <microseconds> \r\n                              Target timeline start in whole microseconds; accepts 1500000 or\r\n                              1500000us\r\n          --duration <microseconds> \r\n                              Target duration in whole microseconds; accepts 1500000 or\r\n                              1500000us\r\n          --source-start-time <microseconds> \r\n                              Source audio start in whole microseconds; accepts 1500000 or\r\n                              1500000us\r\n          --source-duration <microseconds> \r\n                              Source audio duration in whole microseconds; accepts 1500000 or\r\n                              1500000us\r\n          --target-track-index TEXT \r\n                              Target audio track index\r\n          --replace TEXT      Replace existing text-reading audio bound to the target: true /\r\n                              false\r\n          --provider-params-json TEXT \r\n                              Provider-specific parameters as a JSON object or @path\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Tag a text segment with a happy tone at normal speed\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo text-add-tone --speed 1.0 --emotion happy --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Reuse an existing tone product\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo text-add-tone --resource-id <tone_id> --audio-path /tmp/tone.wav --seg-id <UUID>\r\n",
